{"id":"e01t4","name":"Surge Window Detector","lang":"python","entry":"solution","params":["requests","window"],"limit_s":4,"ordered":true,"desc":"<p>The pricing team turns on \"surge pricing\" when demand is unusually high. You are given the timestamps (in seconds, not sorted) of all ride requests of one day in <code>requests</code>, and a window size <code>window</code> in seconds.</p>\n<p>Time is split into aligned windows <code>[0, window)</code>, <code>[window, 2 * window)</code>, and so on. Consider every window from the one that contains the <b>smallest</b> timestamp to the one that contains the <b>largest</b> timestamp, both included, <b>including windows with no request</b>. The <b>average demand</b> is the number of requests divided by the number of these windows.</p>\n<p>A window is a <b>surge window</b> if its number of requests is <b>strictly greater</b> than twice the average demand.</p>\n<p>Your task is to return the list of surge windows as pairs <code>[start, end]</code>, where <code>end = start + window</code>, sorted by <code>start</code>. If <code>requests</code> is empty, return an empty list.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p>For <code>requests = [700, 30, 610, 650, 3500, 1199, 800, 2000, 900], window = 600</code>, the output should be</p><pre class=\"exv\">[[600, 1200]]</pre>\n<p>The windows go from <code>[0, 600)</code> to <code>[3000, 3600)</code>: 6 windows for 9 requests, so the average is <code>1.5</code>. Only <code>[600, 1200)</code> has more than <code>3</code> requests.</p><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 4 seconds (py3)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 1 GB<br><b>[input]</b> array.integer requests<br><b>[input]</b> integer window<br><b>[output]</b> array.array.integer</div>","starter":"def solution(requests, window):\n    # write your code here\n    return []\n","hints":[],"summary_fr":"","tags":["comptage","division","dict","bornes"],"minutes":20,"source":"Kata Lab","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"requests":[700,30,610,650,3500,1199,800,2000,900],"window":600},"expected":{"value":[[600,1200]]}},{"input":{"requests":[5,5,5,5],"window":600},"expected":{"value":[]}}],"hidden_n":10,"hidden":"","solution":""}